---
permalink: /public/sitemap.xml
eleventyExcludeFromCollections: true
---
{#-
  sitemap.xml, written by the build.

  THE PERMALINK GOES THROUGH public/ ON PURPOSE, and /public/ is not part of the
  served path. The Vite plugin renames Eleventy's output to a temp folder and
  rebuilds with emptyOutDir, discarding anything it does not reference, and a
  plain sitemap.xml sitting in the output root is exactly that. Vite copies its
  publicDir verbatim to the output root, so this lands at /sitemap.xml. Same
  route robots.txt, _headers, _redirects and site.webmanifest take, and the same
  reason: passthrough alone silently lost all of them. See src/robots.njk, which
  records this being learned the hard way.

  eleventyExcludeFromCollections keeps this file out of collections.all, which
  is the set it iterates. Without it the sitemap lists itself.

  ============================================================
  WHAT IS IN IT, AND WHERE THAT DECISION LIVES.
  ============================================================

  collections.all, filtered by pageNoindex. Not a hand-maintained list, and not
  a purpose-built collection either. eleventy.config.js already recorded the
  reasoning for whoever wrote this file: the sitemap wants every URL on the
  site, which is not the union of the two article collections, and Eleventy
  already maintains exactly that set. A third collection would be a narrower
  answer to this template's question and a second thing to keep in step.

  THE EXCLUSION IS NOT DECIDED HERE. It is decided by pageNoindex, which is the
  same value base.njk uses to emit the robots meta tag. That is deliberate and it
  is the point of the whole arrangement: a page cannot be noindexed and in the
  sitemap at the same time, because both facts come from one boolean. Adding a
  reason to hold a page back is one edit in tools/eleventy/page-noindex.js and it
  covers both. There is no list to maintain in this file and nothing here to
  forget.

  /yelp-map/ is excluded twice over, which is belt and braces rather than
  duplication: it carries noindex: true, which pageNoindex reads, AND
  eleventyExcludeFromCollections, which keeps it out of the set below entirely.
  Its front matter calls those ways one and two of four.

  ============================================================
  NO lastmod. DELIBERATE, NOT AN OMISSION.
  ============================================================

  The protocol makes it optional and Google states it ignores the value unless
  it is consistently accurate. This build cannot be consistently accurate: only
  articles carry a date in front matter, the ten marketing pages carry none, and
  Eleventy's page.date falls back to file mtime, which a fresh clone resets to
  checkout time. So the honest options were a real date on a third of the URLs
  and a checkout timestamp on the rest, or nothing. Nothing is better than a
  field that lies on every deploy.

  changefreq and priority are absent for the same reason and a stronger one:
  Google has said publicly it ignores both entirely.

  ============================================================
  WHY IT EMPTIES RATHER THAN DISAPPEARING ON A NON-LIVE DEPLOY.
  ============================================================

  When deploy.indexable is false, every page on the deploy carries
  noindex, nofollow. A populated sitemap would then contradict every single URL
  it lists, and it would be submitting a preview host's copies of pages that
  compete with production. So the URLs are withheld.

  The FILE still exists, at the same path, on every deploy. Emitting nothing
  would make /sitemap.xml a 404 on preview and a 200 on production, and a path
  that flaps between the two is a worse thing to hand a monitor or a crawler
  than one that consistently answers "nothing here yet" with a reason attached.
-#}
<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
{% if deploy.indexable -%}
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
{%- for entry in collections.all %}
{%- if not entry.data.pageNoindex %}
  <url>
    <loc>{{ entry.url | absoluteUrl | escape }}</loc>
  </url>
{%- endif %}
{%- endfor %}
</urlset>
{%- else -%}
<!--
  NOT the production deploy ({{ deploy.branch or "local build" }}).

  Deliberately empty. Every page on this deploy carries a noindex meta tag, so
  listing any of them here would contradict the page itself and submit a host
  that must not compete with production. The file is present at the same path on
  every deploy so this URL never flaps between 200 and 404.

  Populated on a Cloudflare Pages deploy of the production branch with
  SITE_LIVE=1, and on nothing else. See src/_data/deploy.js.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
</urlset>
{%- endif %}
